WEBVTT

00:08.530 --> 00:10.540
There are not many things that are certain.

00:10.850 --> 00:13.950
With devotion and diligence, I tread

00:13.950 --> 00:18.120
upon a desert of certainty and uncertainty.

00:19.510 --> 00:21.650
My name is Franz Schubert.

00:21.920 --> 00:23.800
But is this certain?

00:24.090 --> 00:27.470
And there is one more answer
that I seek obsessively:

00:33.150 --> 00:35.700
Where am I?

02:21.870 --> 02:25.910
04: "Wandering Kouhai"

02:22.530 --> 02:25.910
This world is not the
same as the one I knew.

02:27.100 --> 02:29.790
Peculiar, disorderly, and bewitching.

02:30.770 --> 02:32.930
This must be some kind of trap.

02:33.740 --> 02:34.920
Otherwise,

02:35.480 --> 02:37.560
there couldn't be so many people.

02:40.820 --> 02:43.850
The poem by Goethe to which I created music,

02:44.430 --> 02:46.350
Der Erlkönig...

02:49.220 --> 02:50.310
<i>Erlking</i>...

02:50.680 --> 02:53.810
He must have been displeased
with the piece I wrote.

02:54.320 --> 02:57.740
He's created a phantom to capture my mind

02:57.740 --> 02:59.820
and make me forget my purpose.

03:00.630 --> 03:03.750
But I shall never forget

03:03.750 --> 03:05.160
about that man.

03:09.100 --> 03:10.090
He got away!

03:10.090 --> 03:11.250
Over there!

03:13.910 --> 03:15.300
Split up!

03:15.300 --> 03:16.250
That way!

03:24.340 --> 03:25.140
That's...

03:27.190 --> 03:30.510
Those proud eyes, his overwhelming
aura of majesty...

03:30.810 --> 03:33.400
He appears different, but
there's no mistaking it.

03:33.800 --> 03:36.150
It's the master of my soul.

03:36.760 --> 03:38.380
Beethoven-senpai!

03:42.630 --> 03:45.590
The only thing certain in
this phantom world is that

03:45.940 --> 03:49.410
Beethoven-senpai exists
somewhere in it.

03:49.740 --> 03:52.240
The single glimmer of
light lighting my path.

03:52.660 --> 03:54.730
I must find and meet with him,

03:54.230 --> 03:58.340
Thanks, young man, you're a life saver.

03:54.730 --> 03:57.090
even if I must search to
the ends of the land.

03:58.190 --> 03:59.730
Beautiful scenery,

04:00.400 --> 04:02.220
heartwarming smiles...

04:03.930 --> 04:05.610
But I must not be deceived.

04:06.620 --> 04:08.430
This pleasant old man is one of

04:08.960 --> 04:10.430
the Erlking's minions.

04:11.670 --> 04:14.100
Everyone in this world

04:14.100 --> 04:16.130
receives orders from the Erlking.

04:16.130 --> 04:18.330
They attempt to confuse me.

04:20.570 --> 04:21.290
No.

04:22.200 --> 04:24.470
Perhaps everyone here is being deceived by

04:24.790 --> 04:26.910
the Erlking, to be entrapped in this world.

04:28.630 --> 04:30.090
Welcome.

04:32.360 --> 04:34.030
Thank you very much.

04:34.900 --> 04:36.230
Welcome.

04:36.950 --> 04:38.680
Thank you very much.

04:39.120 --> 04:40.250
Welcome.

04:41.110 --> 04:42.890
Thank you very much.

04:42.890 --> 04:47.010
What's amazing is that there's
music all throughout the land.

04:47.010 --> 04:49.010
Golden Fair

04:47.620 --> 04:49.010
You're in the way, mister.

05:02.110 --> 05:03.690
Where're you headed?

05:05.610 --> 05:09.700
Daiei-maru

05:06.880 --> 05:09.700
The many strange, enticing pieces of

05:09.700 --> 05:12.220
music all capture my heart.

05:12.540 --> 05:15.710
It makes me want to drown in this world.

05:16.880 --> 05:18.710
Pleasure and chaos.

05:18.710 --> 05:19.930
No, don't do this.

05:19.930 --> 05:21.380
Open your eyes, Franz.

05:28.860 --> 05:31.970
What? You don't know which one you got on?

05:32.530 --> 05:34.620
My name is Franz Schubert.

05:34.990 --> 05:36.280
I shall push forward.

05:36.280 --> 05:39.000
With diligence and devotion.

05:39.300 --> 05:41.660
Until the day I find Beethoven-senpai.

05:47.320 --> 05:49.290
The infantilization continues.

05:49.660 --> 05:52.600
People are returning to
a baby-like state en masse

05:52.600 --> 05:55.030
in this "infantilization phenomenon."

05:52.740 --> 06:02.040
Mysterious Infantilization Phenomenon Spreads...

05:55.030 --> 05:58.430
Though the cause is still
uncertain, it's become clear that

05:58.430 --> 06:02.040
the occurrences are slowly
spreading eastward.

06:02.320 --> 06:04.140
Such a weird story.

06:04.140 --> 06:07.890
Huh, there's going to be a
gyoza stamp rally this summer.

06:07.890 --> 06:09.470
What's a stamp rally?

06:09.470 --> 06:16.430
Hamamatsu Festival
Stamp Rally!

06:09.900 --> 06:11.910
You go around eating at
different gyoza shops,

06:11.910 --> 06:13.970
and you collect stamps.

06:14.270 --> 06:16.430
And once you get ten
stamps, you get a prize.

06:17.490 --> 06:19.520
So it's like a picnic.

06:19.880 --> 06:22.260
A voyage in pursuit of gyoza.

06:24.550 --> 06:27.210
A battle between the wizards of flames!

06:27.540 --> 06:30.070
I have but to prevail!

06:30.530 --> 06:32.420
Are there going to be lots of girls?

06:32.420 --> 06:33.650
Yeah, probably.

06:33.650 --> 06:35.240
There's a kite-flying competition and stuff.

06:35.240 --> 06:36.750
It's a pretty big festival.

06:36.750 --> 06:38.170
Let's go, then!

06:38.170 --> 06:39.120
What? Me, too?

06:39.120 --> 06:42.460
Who else is going to pay for it, Sousuke?

06:42.460 --> 06:43.840
<i>You</i> pay for it.

06:44.420 --> 06:45.580
You're coming, too, right, Kanae?

06:45.580 --> 06:46.700
I'm not going.

06:46.700 --> 06:49.150
Why not? Why not? Come on!

06:49.150 --> 06:51.920
I'm going to be so bored without you.

06:51.920 --> 06:54.400
I have to clean and do the
laundry and fix the walls and

06:54.400 --> 06:56.950
fix the floors and fix the ceilings.

06:56.950 --> 06:59.640
I have a ton of work backed
up, thanks to <i>some people</i>.

06:59.910 --> 07:01.270
Who? Sousuke?

07:01.270 --> 07:02.760
She said some <i>people</i>.

07:04.360 --> 07:06.520
This town is familiar.

07:06.520 --> 07:09.150
That building that looks
like a massive harmonica...

07:11.170 --> 07:12.320
Isn't it...

07:15.080 --> 07:16.000
Let's move it.

07:16.000 --> 07:17.350
All right.

07:18.700 --> 07:21.790
Are they preparing for a large ball?

07:22.240 --> 07:22.830
No,

07:22.830 --> 07:26.800
Festival

07:23.490 --> 07:26.800
that must be the uniform of this world.

07:27.980 --> 07:30.800
We may see the ascension of a new king.

07:31.760 --> 07:33.910
Beethoven-senpai might be here.

07:47.850 --> 07:48.870
Is this...

07:49.740 --> 07:50.990
A music box?

07:59.620 --> 08:01.350
This piece!

08:01.350 --> 08:02.890
It's by Beethoven-senpai!

08:03.650 --> 08:05.250
What a revelation!

08:05.550 --> 08:07.290
Even in this strange land,

08:07.290 --> 08:10.210
Senpai's great works resound throughout.

08:10.520 --> 08:11.220
Amazing.

08:11.560 --> 08:12.960
Too amazing.

08:15.290 --> 08:16.910
An impressive music box.

08:16.910 --> 08:18.720
It must sound equally impressive.

08:31.540 --> 08:33.850
This is Mozart's...

08:35.860 --> 08:39.190
Your music is nothing but
an imitation of Mozart's.

08:39.190 --> 08:41.410
S-Salieri-sensei...

08:41.410 --> 08:42.430
A rip-off.

08:42.430 --> 08:43.980
Quit ripping people off!

08:44.310 --> 08:46.080
Those days of humiliation...

08:47.980 --> 08:51.050
You won't get away with this, Mozart!

08:53.140 --> 08:55.930
Bravo, Beethoven-senpai!

08:56.230 --> 08:58.550
And you, curse be upon you, Mozart!

09:00.740 --> 09:02.310
Oh man, simul-sneeze.

09:02.550 --> 09:04.730
I had the chills just now.

09:04.730 --> 09:05.720
I did as well.

09:05.720 --> 09:07.640
The fury of the wizards of flames must be

09:07.640 --> 09:09.770
making my senses tremble with excitement.

09:09.770 --> 09:11.570
Gyoza Stamp Rally

09:10.200 --> 09:13.730
We're just going to the gyoza
shops to eat gyoza, you know.

09:11.570 --> 09:12.690
Gyoza Stamp Rally

09:11.610 --> 09:12.690
44th Hamamatsu Festival

09:12.690 --> 09:14.780
44th Hamamatsu Festival

09:21.370 --> 09:23.370
Oranges

09:23.370 --> 09:28.290
Oranges

09:23.670 --> 09:25.980
It's important to get out of that

09:25.980 --> 09:28.290
musty room to catch some sunlight.

09:28.650 --> 09:32.210
A limitless blessing, raining
down upon all living creatures.

09:32.840 --> 09:34.630
This is love, don't you think?

09:38.140 --> 09:41.260
Master Gyoza

09:49.190 --> 09:51.110
This, too, is music.

09:51.650 --> 09:53.560
Opening with the steaming adagio,

09:53.560 --> 09:56.360
transitioning suddenly into
a sizzling, wild allegro.

09:56.750 --> 09:58.490
And the dal segno.

09:58.960 --> 09:59.820
Impressive.

10:00.610 --> 10:04.370
That man would be qualified to
conduct at the royal chambers.

10:05.540 --> 10:07.250
It's good. Want a bite?

10:08.170 --> 10:09.030
Thank you.

10:09.440 --> 10:10.540
Here you are.

10:10.850 --> 10:12.000
The stamps are there.

10:27.200 --> 10:29.680
Nymphs are dancing in my mouth!

10:29.680 --> 10:31.430
This is poetry.

10:31.430 --> 10:32.230
Indeed!

10:34.450 --> 10:36.490
You are truly an artist!

10:38.150 --> 10:39.700
Sure, thanks.

10:40.310 --> 10:41.060
Goodbye.

10:41.060 --> 10:43.470
Hey, pay up!

10:48.010 --> 10:49.870
You better work hard.

10:49.870 --> 10:51.500
I'm going for a smoke.

10:51.850 --> 10:53.880
Don't you dare try to run.

10:54.620 --> 10:55.330
Yes, sir.

10:59.530 --> 11:02.300
Adagio. Allegro. Dal segno.

11:02.810 --> 11:03.730
No.

11:03.730 --> 11:07.520
I know this is the work of the
Erlking, but I can't stop myself.

11:20.430 --> 11:22.050
A singing gyoza shop?

11:22.050 --> 11:23.410
That's kind of cool.

11:23.780 --> 11:25.700
Excuse me, I'd like one.

11:31.260 --> 11:32.060
It's good.

11:32.360 --> 11:33.670
I'll have one, too.

11:34.120 --> 11:35.300
Two for me.

11:35.300 --> 11:36.590
Three for me.

11:37.050 --> 11:39.460
Wow, look at that line.

11:39.460 --> 11:40.320
Very well.

11:40.320 --> 11:41.590
We'll begin here.

11:52.640 --> 11:55.110
This song sounds kind of familiar.

11:55.670 --> 11:56.770
"Heidenröslein."

11:57.530 --> 11:59.930
One of Franz Schubert's

11:58.030 --> 12:04.620
Franz Schubert

11:59.930 --> 12:01.960
most famous pieces,

12:01.960 --> 12:05.770
like "Der Erlkönig," it's
based on a poem by Goethe.

12:06.070 --> 12:09.040
You seriously don't know this
piece? What are you, st—

12:09.450 --> 12:13.040
Beethoven-senpai, where are you?

12:13.920 --> 12:15.260
This song...

12:15.590 --> 12:18.020
That gyoza at the other place was good, too.

12:18.020 --> 12:20.540
It's browned just right.

12:20.540 --> 12:21.370
Browned?

12:21.670 --> 12:24.800
What if the elusive gyoza I seek is there?

12:25.210 --> 12:26.390
I must find out.

12:26.390 --> 12:28.410
What? After you waited
in line all this time?

12:28.410 --> 12:30.060
Let him go, I guess.

12:30.320 --> 12:32.120
I'll have a pack.

12:32.120 --> 12:34.020
Aren't you having any?

12:34.020 --> 12:35.580
We're sharing it.

12:35.580 --> 12:37.010
I don't have that much money.

12:38.090 --> 12:38.910
What the...

12:38.910 --> 12:40.670
The moment I look at this man's face...

12:41.610 --> 12:42.680
I get chills.

12:42.680 --> 12:43.670
What?

12:43.670 --> 12:45.660
Is there something on my face?

12:45.960 --> 12:46.700
No.

12:47.240 --> 12:47.870
Here you are.

12:48.540 --> 12:51.530
I don't want to see this man ever again.

12:52.320 --> 12:54.640
Man, that was good.

12:55.760 --> 12:57.630
I'm bored now.

12:57.630 --> 12:58.820
All right, break a leg.

12:59.140 --> 13:02.180
Girls! Girls!

12:59.750 --> 13:01.810
How selfish can you get?

13:03.440 --> 13:05.630
Hey, have you seen Cho-chan?

13:06.030 --> 13:07.500
No, I haven't seen him.

13:07.500 --> 13:09.880
I finally dragged him out to a picnic,

13:09.880 --> 13:11.770
but we've lost each other somehow.

13:12.020 --> 13:13.030
Sure.

13:13.630 --> 13:15.710
You'll help me find him, won't you?

13:15.710 --> 13:16.730
Huh?

13:17.850 --> 13:19.700
Look at this line you've made.

13:19.700 --> 13:21.610
You've got some talent.

13:22.160 --> 13:23.260
Good work.

13:23.650 --> 13:26.070
Don't go eating without money anymore.

13:27.500 --> 13:29.800
My moment of bliss...

13:30.560 --> 13:31.870
No, wait.

13:31.870 --> 13:33.670
Get it together, Franz.

13:34.120 --> 13:35.800
Don't forget your purpose.

13:36.320 --> 13:37.890
Let's depart once again.

13:38.350 --> 13:42.000
To find my light, Beethoven-senpai.

13:55.440 --> 13:58.310
Hasshie, time to eat.

14:13.190 --> 14:16.330
It's so nice without those
noisy freeloaders around.

14:23.260 --> 14:26.170
Was this house ever this quiet?

14:26.900 --> 14:28.960
It's a bit lonely, maybe?

14:29.260 --> 14:30.620
Nah, no way.

14:30.620 --> 14:32.160
I think I'll read a book.

14:35.420 --> 14:37.140
Why are you here?

14:37.440 --> 14:39.310
Too many people. Scary.

14:46.860 --> 14:49.150
Wh-What do you want?!

14:49.150 --> 14:52.330
Why is this land so full of language?

14:49.450 --> 14:50.520
Hey, you!

14:50.820 --> 14:52.660
What are you doing there?

14:53.100 --> 14:56.160
Why is that man singing inside a box?

14:58.090 --> 14:59.890
Little children, gathered,

14:59.890 --> 15:02.530
to have music instilled into their bodies.

15:03.090 --> 15:04.710
Is my music of any value

15:05.430 --> 15:08.170
in this incredible world?

15:09.380 --> 15:13.140
A man wandered onto your
property unannounced?

15:13.370 --> 15:17.600
I see. A creepy man danced
while watching the children?

15:17.920 --> 15:19.530
Dining without money?

15:19.530 --> 15:23.110
Yeah, I let him off the hook because
he said he'd pay in labor.

15:23.430 --> 15:26.110
But that bastard was
giving away gyoza for free.

15:26.330 --> 15:29.920
He said, "You won't get away
with it," with a fierce face?

15:29.920 --> 15:30.710
Yeah.

15:30.710 --> 15:33.120
Multiple suspicious
individuals on the loose.

15:33.430 --> 15:35.130
Requesting backup.

15:43.610 --> 15:44.540
Go!

15:44.540 --> 15:45.750
Do it!

15:46.160 --> 15:47.810
Beethoven-senpai,

15:48.240 --> 15:50.620
what are you doing right
now in this labyrinth?

15:50.990 --> 15:54.890
What kind of music do you
see with your proud eyes?

15:52.760 --> 15:55.180
Gyoza Stamp Rally

15:55.870 --> 15:57.850
Few stores remain.

15:58.360 --> 16:01.810
Yet none of them come close
to the taste that I seek.

16:02.760 --> 16:05.610
How deep the world of gyoza is.

16:06.080 --> 16:08.070
Hey, check it out.

16:08.430 --> 16:11.780
This year's kite fights
are going to get heavy.

16:12.870 --> 16:14.850
Might this be some kind of ceremony?

16:16.190 --> 16:18.830
Might Beethoven-senpai be
watching that somewhere?

16:22.200 --> 16:23.500
Ow...

16:23.500 --> 16:24.790
Are you okay?

16:25.180 --> 16:27.560
Hey, you're from that gyoza shop.

16:28.800 --> 16:30.580
Looking for someone, huh?

16:30.580 --> 16:31.360
Yes.

16:31.360 --> 16:33.460
He's a great master of music,

16:33.460 --> 16:35.550
comparable to God in my eyes.

16:35.550 --> 16:36.710
God? really?

16:36.710 --> 16:38.800
One could call him a
genius above the clouds.

16:39.100 --> 16:42.600
He's worlds apart from those <i>other</i> geniuses

16:42.600 --> 16:45.560
who drown in their own talent,

16:45.560 --> 16:47.140
wasting away in selfish pleasures,

16:47.140 --> 16:49.110
imposing upon all the musicians who follow.

16:49.520 --> 16:51.230
Yeah, I know what you mean.

16:51.230 --> 16:53.320
Doesn't it piss you off
when a talented musician

16:53.320 --> 16:56.090
wastes all their time playing around?

16:56.390 --> 16:58.550
I believe we will make good friends.

16:58.970 --> 17:00.010
Yeah?

17:00.010 --> 17:01.610
I'm Kagura Sousuke.

17:01.610 --> 17:02.450
You're...

17:02.450 --> 17:03.860
My name is Schu—

17:04.440 --> 17:08.210
No, should I not introduce my
whole name, Franz Schubert?

17:08.570 --> 17:10.400
Shuu-san. Got it. Nice to meet you.

17:10.800 --> 17:13.200
Man, I have to admit, though,

17:13.200 --> 17:15.440
I'd love to meet that kind of musician,
so I could learn from them.

17:16.120 --> 17:17.390
Do you create music, as well?

17:18.260 --> 17:19.350
Uh-huh.

17:24.310 --> 17:27.940
Oh, Beethoven-senpai, this is the thing.

17:28.240 --> 17:30.280
There's some talent which, no matter

17:30.280 --> 17:33.350
how much effort is put into
it, will never ascend.

17:33.350 --> 17:34.320
Mediocrity.

17:34.680 --> 17:38.050
Bless this young man,
who chases after genius,

17:38.350 --> 17:40.330
only to be met by repeated despair.

17:44.260 --> 17:45.530
Was it <i>that</i> good?

17:45.530 --> 17:47.650
I can't help but tear up.

17:47.650 --> 17:49.040
Seriously?!

17:49.650 --> 17:52.050
Okay, I'm looking for someone, too, so...

17:53.970 --> 17:57.210
Even if I may not reach you,
I shall continue after you,

17:57.530 --> 18:00.050
in the footsteps of your
greatness, Beethoven-senpai.

18:11.730 --> 18:14.230
Rhythm. And chaos.

18:14.580 --> 18:15.650
I feel it.

18:15.650 --> 18:17.680
I'm getting closer to Senpai.

18:18.730 --> 18:20.240
Beethoven-senpai!

18:20.890 --> 18:21.700
'Sup.

18:21.700 --> 18:23.650
Th-This man!

18:23.650 --> 18:25.910
Are you here to hook up
with some girls, too?

18:25.910 --> 18:27.570
Um... Can I call you Glasses?

18:27.570 --> 18:29.020
Leave me alone!

18:29.020 --> 18:30.310
Don't come near me!

18:30.310 --> 18:31.340
Why are you running away?

18:31.560 --> 18:33.510
Are we, like, playing tag?

18:33.510 --> 18:35.330
I said, "stay away!"

18:35.330 --> 18:36.780
You incarnate of the Erlking!

18:36.780 --> 18:38.280
There's a fight.

18:38.280 --> 18:39.470
That man...

18:39.470 --> 18:41.480
Beige clothes and circular glasses.

18:41.480 --> 18:42.990
Frazzly red hair.

18:42.990 --> 18:44.470
Isn't that the suspicious individual?

18:44.470 --> 18:46.230
All right, get them both!

18:46.630 --> 18:48.030
Gotcha!

18:49.690 --> 18:50.870
Let me go!

18:50.870 --> 18:51.900
You, stop!

18:52.230 --> 18:53.760
Stay calm!

18:53.760 --> 18:56.220
What's up? Wanna join us?

18:56.220 --> 18:58.200
Oh no, it's the Erlking's army!

18:58.630 --> 19:01.200
They're trying to stop me here.

19:02.630 --> 19:03.490
Could that mean...

19:03.760 --> 19:04.980
You're here, aren't you?!

19:04.980 --> 19:06.620
Beethoven-senpai!

19:06.990 --> 19:07.960
Senpai?

19:08.430 --> 19:10.920
I've been looking for you!

19:10.920 --> 19:13.300
Senpai!

19:13.670 --> 19:15.000
Chopin.

19:15.000 --> 19:17.170
Beethoven-senpai!

19:17.410 --> 19:20.260
I feel you near!

19:20.260 --> 19:21.840
Gyoza Stamp Rally

19:20.500 --> 19:21.840
Say what?!

19:21.840 --> 19:24.760
Sorry, it was more popular than we expected.

19:21.840 --> 19:26.520
This Year's Prize

19:21.840 --> 19:26.520
Out of Stock

19:24.760 --> 19:26.520
We just ran out.

19:26.520 --> 19:31.690
Prize Exchange

19:28.010 --> 19:31.690
Search as I may, I remain unrewarded.

19:32.060 --> 19:36.380
Is this fate?!

19:44.080 --> 19:47.830
Beethoven-senpai!

19:48.130 --> 19:51.520
Lässt unsere Musik

19:51.820 --> 19:54.790
erklingen!

19:55.340 --> 19:56.590
I proceed.

19:57.380 --> 20:00.720
Step by step, as though on a journey.

20:01.420 --> 20:04.920
I place each note, carefully
and with certainty.

20:05.680 --> 20:09.440
Thusly, I shall carry on
down the path of my Musik.

20:16.260 --> 20:18.510
Schubert's "Lullaby."

20:18.510 --> 20:20.200
Lyricist unknown.

20:20.200 --> 20:24.160
Said to be dedicated to
his beloved mothe— hey!

20:41.170 --> 20:42.270
Sousuke!

20:42.590 --> 20:43.810
Sousuke!

20:44.150 --> 20:45.700
Does not compute.

20:45.700 --> 20:48.000
Conventional wisdom dictates that a

20:48.000 --> 20:50.560
high school behaving like
an infant is very creepy.

20:52.870 --> 20:55.150
Beethoven-senpai!

20:59.140 --> 21:00.570
What was I...

21:01.840 --> 21:02.730
Not again.

21:02.730 --> 21:04.030
It's this situation again.

21:07.190 --> 21:10.490
This has happened several times before.

21:11.360 --> 21:13.290
No, this isn't the time.

21:15.960 --> 21:17.350
Beethoven-senpai.

21:19.290 --> 21:21.590
I see you're being silly.

21:23.960 --> 21:25.840
But we finally meet!

21:32.520 --> 21:34.770
Bee... tho—

21:41.670 --> 21:44.400
There you are, Cho-chan.

21:44.700 --> 21:46.190
Why are you so afraid?

21:46.190 --> 21:48.410
People are all connected through love.

21:48.710 --> 21:50.950
I'd rather we connect through the Internet.

21:51.760 --> 21:54.660
Beethoven-senpai!

21:56.580 --> 21:57.960
The weather's so nice.

22:01.100 --> 22:01.630
Huh?

22:19.550 --> 22:21.900
What happened yesterday?

22:21.900 --> 22:24.850
Was that the infantilization phenomenon
that's apparently going around?

22:24.850 --> 22:26.200
That was so fun.

22:26.200 --> 22:27.280
Win a Gyouna-kun mug!

22:27.450 --> 22:29.660
Gyoza Stamp Rally

22:28.010 --> 22:29.660
I won't depend on others.

22:30.010 --> 22:32.930
I'll create the elusive
flavor with my own hands.

22:31.200 --> 22:35.090
Midnight Japan time, the
infantilization phenomenon

22:33.660 --> 22:40.420
Infantilization Phenomenon in Eastern Africa

22:35.090 --> 22:36.990
was discovered in eastern Africa.

22:36.990 --> 22:40.420
A Japanese kite was found
nearby, for some reason.

22:40.790 --> 22:44.880
The local Japanese embassy
is currently investigating.

22:41.150 --> 22:43.250
Such a weird situation.

24:15.970 --> 24:27.520
05: Jet-Black Gyoza

24:16.280 --> 24:18.770
Is it the skin? The filling?
The frying? The kneading?

24:18.770 --> 24:20.150
Is it the sweetness? Or the spiciness?

24:20.150 --> 24:22.570
Does it boil down to existentialism
or structuralism?

24:22.570 --> 24:26.570
The mystery of the gyoza being
pursued by the struggling genius intellect

24:26.570 --> 24:29.180
shall soon be answered.
